1: // =========================================================
2: // LF_PowerGrid - Electrical Graph (v1.0)
3: //
4: // In-memory directed graph of the electrical network.
5: // Nodes = devices, edges = wires. Rebuilt from wire data at
6: // startup, maintained incrementally during runtime.
7: //
8: // NOT persisted — wires are the source of truth.
9: // Server-only: all public methods are guarded by #ifdef SERVER.
10: //
11: // === POWER ALLOCATION (v1.0) ===
12: // Binary all-off policy: if totalDemand > availableOutput on any
13: // distributor node, ALL downstream of that node receives 0.
14: // AllocateOutput (~90 lines) is the sole allocation function.
15: // Overload state is per-node (m_Overloaded bool), not per-edge.
16: // PASSTHROUGH always reports real demand (self + downstream) via
17: // m_LastStableOutput, even when unpowered — prevents oscillation.
18: //
19: // === KEY SUBSYSTEMS ===
20: // - ProcessDirtyQueue: BFS propagation with node+edge budgets,
21: //   requeue limits, and deferred requeue for deep chains.
22: // - AllocateOutput: binary demand/allocation on outgoing edges.
23: //   Multi-source split via CountPoweredIncoming (Combiner pattern).
24: // - SyncNodeToEntity: syncs LoadRatio+Overloaded (SOURCE),
25: //   Powered+Overloaded (PASSTHROUGH), Powered (CONSUMER/CAMERA).
26: // - ValidateConsumerStates: bidirectional zombie/dark detection.
27: // - PostBulkRebuild: type-aware orphan SyncVar reset.
28: //
29: // === ANTI-OSCILLATION ===
30: // PASSTHROUGH demand signal = downstreamDemand + selfConsumption,
31: // always written to m_LastStableOutput regardless of power state.
32: // Demand is a topology property, not a power-flow property.
33: // Cold-start fallback: m_MaxOutput when m_LastStableOutput=0.
34: //
35: // === SAFETY NETS ===
36: // - Component Watchdog: per-subnet node limit (v0.7.31)
37: // - Atomic Graph Mutations: deferred cleanup (v0.7.34)
38: // - Topology-aware downstream propagation (v0.7.38 B1)
39: // - Carryover requeue count reset (v0.7.38 RC-09)
40: // - Deferred requeue for requeue-limit orphans (v0.8.3)
41: // =========================================================
42: 
43: // The 4_World facade exposes the graph contract required by world callers.
44: // Runtime state and implementation bodies are hosted by the mission layer.
45: // A neutral fallback is returned when the mission factory is unavailable.
